<section class="wa-hero"><div class="wa-w wa-hero-g"><div><p class="wa-k">Drawing 00 &middot; General arrangement</p><h1>Choose the right watch, then wear it well.</h1><p class="wa-lead">Watches is an independent guide to wristwatches. We explain case sizes, water resistance ratings, movements and straps in plain, technical language, with tools that measure your wrist and match a watch to your day.</p><ul class="wa-dims"><li><b>38&ndash;42</b><span>mm, the most common case sizes</span></li><li><b>30&ndash;300</b><span>metres, the ratings you will see</span></li><li><b>4</b><span>movement types explained</span></li></ul></div>
