" stroke="#3D5774" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="100" y1="14" x2="100" y2="19" transform="rotate(318 100 100)" stroke="#3D5774" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="100" y1="14" x2="100" y2="19" transform="rotate(324 100 100)" stroke="#3D5774" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="100" y1="12" x2="100" y2="24" transform="rotate(330 100 100)" stroke="#5FD4E8" stroke-width="3"/><line x1="100" y1="14" x2="100" y2="19" transform="rotate(336 100 100)" stroke="#3D5774" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="100" y1="14" x2="100" y2="19" transform="rotate(342 100 100)" stroke="#3D5774" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="100" y1="14" x2="100" y2="19" transform="rotate(348 100 100)" stroke="#3D5774" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="100" y1="14" x2="100" y2="19" transform="rotate(354 100 100)" stroke="#3D5774" stroke-width="1.5"/><line id="hh" x1="100" y1="100" x2="100" y2="54" stroke="#E8EEF5" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round"/><line id="mh" x1="100" y1="100" x2="100" y2="32" stroke="#E8EEF5" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><line id="sh" x1="100" y1="112" x2="100" y2="26" stroke="#F2B544" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="4" fill="#F2B544"/></svg><p class="wa-clk-l"><span id="clk-t">--:--:--</span> local time</p><figure class="wa-spec"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794654639581-276c749e1d3f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=300&q=75" alt="a stainless steel wristwatch with a black dial and rotating bezel" width="420" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Fig. 1 &mdash; Steel diver, black dial, unidirectional bezel</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="wa-s" id="fit"><div class="wa-w wa-fit"><div><p class="wa-k">Drawing 01 &middot; Case fit</p><h2>What size suits your wrist?</h2><p>Measure around your wrist bone with a strip of paper or a soft tape. Then slide to your measurement. The drawing scales the case against your wrist.</p><label for="wf-c" class="wa-lab">Wrist circumference <output id="wf-v">17.0 cm</output></label><input type="range" id="wf-c" min="13" max="23" step="0.5" value="17"><div class="wa-units" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Wrist profile"><label><input type="radio" name="wp" value="flat" checked><span>Flat wrist</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="wp" value="round"><span>Round wrist</span></label></div><dl class="wa-out" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Case diameter</dt><dd id="wf-d">38&ndash;41 mm</dd></div><div><dt>Max lug-to-lug</dt><dd id="wf-l">48 mm</dd></div><div><dt>Strap width</dt><dd id="wf-s">20 mm</dd></div></dl></div>
<div class="wa-draw"><svg viewBox="0 0 360 260" aria-hidden="true"><defs><pattern id="hatch" width="6" height="6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(45)"><line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="6" stroke="#1E3149" stroke-width="2"/></pattern></defs><ellipse id="wr" cx="180" cy="130" rx="150" ry="70" fill="url(#hatch)" stroke="#5FD4E8" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect id="st" x="160" y="20" width="40" height="220" fill="#16263A" stroke="#3D5774"/><rect id="lg" x="150" y="76" width="60" height="108" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="#F2B544" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/><circle id="cs" cx="180" cy="130" r="40" fill="#0B1522" stroke="#E8EEF5" stroke-width="2.5"/><line id="dm" x1="140" y1="130" x2="220" y2="130" stroke="#F2B544" stroke-width="1"/><text id="dt" x="180" y="124" text-anchor="middle" fill="#F2B544" font-size="11" font-family="monospace">40 mm</text><text x="20" y="250" fill="#7F96B2" font-size="10" font-family="monospace">WRIST SECTION &middot; NOT TO SCALE</text></svg></div></div></section>

<section class="wa-s wa-dk2" id="depth"><div class="wa-w wa-dep"><div><p class="wa-k">Drawing 02 &middot; Depth gauge</p><h2>What the water rating really means</h2><p>A watch marked &ldquo;30 m&rdquo; is not built for a 30-metre dive. The number comes from a lab pressure test. Pick what you plan to do and the gauge shows the rating to look for.</p><div class="wa-acts" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Activity"><label><input type="radio" name="act" value="0" checked><span>Hand washing, rain</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="act" value="1"><span>Shower, splashing</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="act" value="2"><span>Swimming laps</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="act" value="3"><span>Snorkelling</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="act" value="4"><span>Scuba diving</span></label></div><p class="wa-dep-o" id="dg-o" aria-live="polite"></p><figure class="wa-dep-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1691865179028-1729b766a5cd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=300&q=75" alt="a wristwatch resting on a table" width="520" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<ol class="wa-gauge" id="dg"><li data-r="0"><b>30 m</b><span>Splash resistant. Rain and hand washing only.</span></li><li data-r="1"><b>50 m</b><span>Light water use. Short showers, no swimming.</span></li><li data-r="2"><b>100 m</b><span>Swimming and surface water sports.</span></li><li data-r="3"><b>200 m</b><span>Snorkelling and serious water use.</span></li><li data-r="4"><b>300 m+</b><span>Built and certified for diving.</span></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="wa-s"><div class="wa-w"><p class="wa-k">Drawing 03 &middot; Movements</p><h2>What is ticking inside?</h2><div class="wa-mv"><div class="wa-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Movement types"><button role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="mv-p" data-m="0">Quartz</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="mv-p" data-m="1">Automatic</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="mv-p" data-m="2">Manual wind</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="mv-p" data-m="3">Solar quartz</button></div><div class="wa-mv-g"><div id="mv-p" role="tabpanel" aria-live="polite"></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788125856710-1ae984195874?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=420&q=75" alt="a watchmaker using a precision screwdriver on a mechanical watch movement" width="560" height="420" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Fig. 3 &mdash; Servicing a mechanical movement under a loupe</figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section>

<section class="wa-s wa-dk2"><div class="wa-w wa-strap"><div class="wa-strap-d"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 320" aria-hidden="true"><rect id="sp1" x="70" y="0" width="60" height="110" rx="6" fill="#6B4226"/><rect id="sp2" x="70" y="210" width="60" height="110" rx="6" fill="#6B4226"/><g id="spx"></g><circle cx="100" cy="160" r="62" fill="#C9D3DE"/><circle cx="100" cy="160" r="52" fill="#0B1522"/><path d="M100 160V122M100 160l24 14" stroke="#E8EEF5" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div><div><p class="wa-k">Drawing 04 &middot; Straps</p><h2>Same watch, four characters</h2><div class="wa-sw" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Strap type"><label><input type="radio" name="sp" value="0" checked><span><i style="background:#6B4226"></i>Leather</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sp" value="1"><span><i style="background:#A9B6C3"></i>Steel bracelet</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sp" value="2"><span><i style="background:#1E1E1E"></i>Rubber</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sp" value="3"><span><i style="background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,#2F4A3A 0 6px,#C8A24A 6px 9px)"></i>Fabric (NATO)</span></label></div><div class="wa-sw-o" id="sp-o" aria-live="polite"></div><figure class="wa-sw-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1703505841379-2f863b201212?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=300&q=75" alt="a wristwatch on a metal link bracelet" width="520" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="wa-s"><div class="wa-w"><p class="wa-k">Drawing 05 &middot; World time</p><h2>One wrist, five cities</h2><p>A second time zone is a common &ldquo;complication&rdquo;. This board shows the same moment around the world.</p><div class="wa-wt" id="wt"></div></div></section>

<section class="wa-s wa-notes"><div class="wa-w wa-nt"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793417160274-267547d0c625?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=480&q=75" alt="a man in a pinstripe suit adjusting his watch" width="640" height="480" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Fig. 6 &mdash; The final check before leaving: crown pushed in, strap snug, not tight.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1772460667113-2010dd647ebe?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=480&q=75" alt="a collection of assorted wristwatches on a brown surface" width="640" height="480" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Fig. 7 &mdash; A rotation of three to five watches covers most needs: one dress, one sport, one everyday.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

